// Everything FCSE.exe carries inside itself, so the loader ships as a single file.
//
// Generated from assets/fcse.rc.in by CMake. The paths are absolute and CMake-substituted because
// rc.exe resolves a relative filename against its working directory, not against this file's own
// location; CMake writes them forward-slashed, which rc.exe accepts, so nothing needs escaping.
//
// Unquoted, non-numeric resource names are string names, so the RCDATA entries below are found with
// FindResourceW(module, L"FCSE_MGB", RT_RCDATA) and there is no resource.h to keep in sync.

// The application icon, built from assets/logo.png by assets/make_icon.py - see that file for which
// sizes it contains and why. It is the one *numeric* resource id here, and it is 1: nothing in FCSE
// looks this up, the shell does, and the shell shows the lowest-numbered RT_GROUP_ICON in the file
// as the exe's icon. A string name would leave that to chance.
1                   ICON   "@FCSE_ICON@"

// Both aspect variants of FCSE's settings-page layout. page_assets.cpp picks between them at runtime
// using the engine's own widescreen flag, and magma_package.cpp serves the bytes to the engine
// through a hooked file reader (nothing in Dunia will open a loose file by path).
//
// These two paths are in the build tree, not in assets/: the layouts are built from
// assets/*.mgb.xml by JackAll's mgb encoder each build, so no built layout is committed.
FCSE_MGB            RCDATA "@FCSE_MGB@"
FCSE_MGB_WIDESCREEN RCDATA "@FCSE_MGB_WIDESCREEN@"

// The script API (src/lua/runtime/fcse.lua), embedded for the same reason as the layouts above:
// there is no loose file for a player to delete or for an installer to leave stale against the exe
// that reads it. lua_host.cpp resolves it as FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME and hands it to require 'fcse'.
FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME    RCDATA "@FCSE_LUA_RUNTIME@"

// The address library: which RVA each stable address ID has in each supported Dunia.dll build.
// Far Cry 2 v1.03 ships as two PC builds with different layouts, so this is what lets one FCSE.exe
// run on both. address_library.cpp expands it once at startup.
//
// A resource rather than a compiled-in array: delta+varint encoded it is ~233 KB against 715 KB of
// raw pairs, and a 2.2 MB translation unit of hex literals was the slowest thing in the build for
// no benefit. Unlike the layouts above this one *is* committed, because building it needs Ghidra
// and both DLLs - see tools/FCSE/tools/addrlib/README.md.
FCSE_ADDRLIB        RCDATA "@FCSE_ADDRLIB@"
